NOTES AND QUESTIONS ON NEELY V. MARTIN K. EBY CONSTRUCTION
The majority opinion in Neely does not go into detail about the evidence presented at trial or the facts of the case, as it was not relevant to the interpretation and application of Rule 50(c)–(e). But Justices Black, Douglas, and Fortas would have reversed on the separate ground that the motion for JNOV (i.e., the renewed motion for judgment as a matter of law) should not have been granted. This issue was not raised in the petition for certiorari, however, and the petitioner had not at any stage in the district court or circuit court requested a new trial. Consequently, the majority opinion held those issues waived in the Supreme Court. Here are the facts and evidence, as recounted by Justice Black:

